We will use the following notation throughout the paper.
• M: target model, or the model to be explained;
• x: a particular sample;
• X or Xj: a group of samples. We will use X to denote
the entire evaluation dataset and Xj to denote the j-th
cohort. {X1, . . . , Xk} is referred as a cohort definition,
which partitions the dataset X into k cohorts;
• ω: a local explanation method. It is data driven and out-
puts local feature importance. Specifically, ωM(X, x) is
the result of evaluating ω in x, on the model M and us-
ing X as context samples. It should treat the target M
as a black-box, i.e., ω does not depend on the specific
architecture of M;
• ej: the explanation for cohort j;
• ax ∈{1, . . . , k}: the cohort assignment for sample x,
representing which cohort x belongs to.
